From 1bd5cd6d9801e2bbb43fc60514b92db79e759acc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:15:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usage): decode speed readings for the run indicator

Show how fast the model decoded: provider output tokens over the decode wall
time (first streamed chunk -> call end), the same quantity DeepSeek Harness
reports. Tool waits and first-token latency stay out of the ratio, and a call
without a recorded first chunk (non-streamed, failed stream, partial stub)
drops out instead of diluting it.

One reading per finished API call, pushed on usage.updated and kept in run
state, where the thinking indicator renders it while the run is live. The
"current" value beside the run average lands in a follow-up patch.

- bridge: forward first_chunk_at from the post_api_request hook
- chat-run: fold provider-timed calls into the run state
- client: run-state reading consumed by the thinking indicator
